; full puzzle: word=NORA-BECS-ALEX, 290x290mm, 61 continuous cut paths (237 edges after dedup)
; generated by emitter.py
; loose-fit: centerline cuts, laser kerf becomes the clearance
; edge dedup: shared cell-cell boundaries cut exactly once
; cut order: letters first, interior next, panel border last
; contiguous edges fused into single continuous cuts (no per-edge re-fire)
; ASSUMES Z already at focal height in your WCS
; warmup: 1000ms = 5.8mm at F350; each cut runs fwd half / back to start first (laser at full power on return), then cuts the whole path at full power
; backtrack budget: 2000ms = 11.7mm — re-trace already-cut line to stay continuous only when it's cheaper than a restart's warmup; longer gaps restart instead (no wholesale double-cut)
; min segment: 0.3mm (shorter chords decimated)
; breakaway bridges: 6 x 0.5mm uncut gaps hold tiny letter counters in place (snap out by hand)
;
;HEAD: laser
;MATERIAL: plywood_veneer_3ply_3mm
;LASER_MODE: static  (M3 — dwell-burn-through risk if motion stalls)

